  "written_utc": "2026-09-24",
  "note": "Version 2 of the Prompt Engineer acceptance cases. The v1 any-of substring groups are replaced by relation specs the oracle checks inside ONE output segment (a line or sentence): 'together' (every group co-located), 'negated' (a negation cue bound to the terms), 'question', 'hedged', 'conditional', 'order', 'count', and 'any' (alternative relations). Each relation names the source 'clause' it protects, so a needs_review result can be checked for surfacing the actual loss. 'forbid' entries may be marked unless_negated ('no code snippets' is not an added code snippet). The oracle (judge in test_prompt_engineer_cases.py) is independent of localflow/v2/transforms/atoms.py.",
  "exposure": "The ten v1 held-out cases (PE-HOLD-001..010) were printed and inspected during the 2026-09-24 M11 audit remediation, before the requirement gate was written. They are marked exposed and moved to split 'regression' here; their held-out score is no longer blind evidence. PE-BLIND-001..010 are new families written on 2026-09-24 before the gate was written, never run against the validator during tuning, and form the blind held-out split. Once they are inspected they must be marked exposed in a new version.",
  "splits": {"dev": 15, "validation": 5, "regression": 10, "held-out": 10},
